<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a>–<a href="/years/1558">1558</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Charles I of Spain, Charles V</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles V was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> ruler who became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> as Charles I in 1516 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in 1519. He inherited the Spanish, Burgundian and Habsburg lands, presiding over the Spanish conquest of the Aztec and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> empires. His reign marked the height of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s European and global power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor" width="250" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Charles_V,_Holy_Roman_Emperor,_seated_(1500%E2%80%931558),_formerly_attributed_to_Titian_(Alte_Pinakothek,_Munich).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Emperor <b>Charles V</b> was born in Ghent in 1500.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-flanders">County of Flanders · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Hainaut became part of the Burgundian Netherlands, passed to the Habsburgs on the death of Mary of Burgundy in 1482, and under <b>Charles V</b> and Philip II belonged to the Seventeen Provinces.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">County of Hainaut · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Under Charles I (r. 1525–1576), who was brought up at the court of Emperor <b>Charles V</b>, the Habsburgs granted the counties of Sigmaringen and Veringen to the house as Austrian fiefs in 1534–1535, after the extinction of the counts of Werdenberg.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-hohenzollern">County of Hohenzollern · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>English victories restored a large Aquitaine under the Treaty of Brétigny in 1360, but the Black Prince's heavy hearth tax led Gascon lords, among them the count of Armagnac, to appeal to <b>Charles V</b> in 1368, and French armies reconquered most of the principality within a decade.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Duchy of Aquitaine · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>It was in Brussels that Emperor <b>Charles V</b> abdicated in 1555 in favour of his son Philip II of Spain.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Breton nobles and soldiers shaped English and French history alike, from the Breton lords of post-Conquest England to Bertrand du Guesclin, constable of France under <b>Charles V</b>, and Olivier de Clisson.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Duchy of Brittany · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>. Died in Monastery of Yuste, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.05,3.73&amp;year=1537" aria-label="Ghent on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4635 394 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5085 664h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5085 664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.05,3.73&amp;year=1537">What was here in 1537? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
